meta {
  name: Reserved path is not a code
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/up
  body: none
  auth: none
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  followRedirects: false
}

tests {
  test("leaves /up to the health check rather than treating it as a code", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  FR-012 from the other side. The catch-all code route is drawn last, so every
  segment the routing table claims wins the match. The same segments are
  enumerated in config/initializers/reserved_paths.rb and refused at creation —
  a code the router would swallow is a code that never redirects.

  The reserved list today: admin, api, assets, favicon, login, logout, packs,
  robots, settings, sidekiq, signup, sitemap, static, up.

  `sidekiq` is reserved in every environment although the Sidekiq dashboard is
  mounted only in development (config/routes.rb). A segment that is a dashboard
  on one machine and a short link on another is the failure the reservation
  exists to prevent, so the list does not vary by environment — and for the same
  reason there is no request here that opens /sidekiq: it would 404 against any
  stack this collection is pointed at other than a development one.
}
